  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The deal sits inside the acceptable ranges on S1, S3, S4 and S5, but S2 is weakened: the 55 °C test with a 5% figure is only a notification/corrective-action/retest trigger and never prohibits sale, so Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%) stays on the market, while per-model numeric failure rates go to purchasers and regulators but not the general public. S5 keeps a mandatory numeric recall at 8 per 100,000 with 48-hour customer notice (biting on Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9), subject to a regulator-approved equally protective alternative. S3's six-year retrofit deadline and S4's 36-month suppression start are the red-line compromise; S1's 30-day deadline for non-serious incidents is the loosest element."
 },
